          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"5-4\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_2\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Most core activities are represented, but the initial purchase is omitted and treasurer checking is duplicated/misplaced after payment, adding unsupported behavior.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Required precedence is broken: corrected reports do not reliably return to supervisor review, and an extra treasurer check is placed after payment instead of before it.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Branch continuation and recurrence are wrong: both correction loops are misrouted, approved/accepted processing continues incorrectly through a merge to another treasurer check, and some exits bypass required approval/payment behavior.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"mixed_or_cascading\",\"explanation\":\"The source requires any returned report to go back to the employee for correction and then again to supervisor review before any further treasurer handling; only after treasurer acceptance does payment occur, followed by waiting for confirmation and ending. In the generated graph, the supervisor-rejection loop cycles between rejection and employee resubmission without returning to the supervisor approval decision, the treasurer-return loop cycles back to the treasurer-return action instead of routing back through supervisor review, and a merge sends even the accepted-and-paid path to another treasurer check before termination. These defects change the core rework, approval, and completion behavior of the whole process, not just local labels.\",\"overall_score\":0.3,\"severity\":\"major\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
